      "id": "md2025_2293",
      "subset": "S5",
      "task_type": "cross-company-year-hybrid",
      "question": "Calculate the percentage increase in NFLX's total revenues from FY2022 to FY2024 and the percentage increase in paid memberships over the same period. How do these growth rates compare, and what does META's FY2022 and FY2024 MD&A provide for user or revenue metrics?",
      "expected_answer": "NFLX total revenues grew from $31,615,550 thousand in FY2022 to $39,000,966 thousand in FY2024, a 23.4% increase ($39,000,966 - $31,615,550) / $31,615,550 * 100 = 23.35%). Paid memberships at end of period grew from 230,747 thousand to 301,626 thousand, a 30.7% increase (($301,626 - $230,747) / $230,747 * 100 = 30.73%). Revenue grew slower than membership base, indicating ARPU pressure or mix shift. META's Item 7 for both FY2022 and FY2024 provides only introductory text with forward-looking statements, no revenue or user metrics, so no comparable data exists in the provided documents.",
      "predicted_answer": "NFLX total revenues rose 23.4% from FY2022 ($31,615,550 thousand) [F1][E3] to FY2024 ($39,000,966 thousand) [F2][E2], while paid memberships grew 30.7% from 230,747 thousand [F3][E3] to 301,626 thousand [F4][E2]. Membership growth therefore outpaced revenue growth by about 7.3 percentage points [C1][C2].\n\nMETA's FY2022 Item 7 discloses worldwide ARPP of $31.79, down 6% from 2021, and discusses Facebook DAU/MAU user metrics, excluding Instagram and WhatsApp [F5][E4]. META's FY2024 Item 7 reports total revenue of $164,501 million, with comparative 2023 ($134,902 million) and 2022 ($116,609 million) figures [F6][E5].",
